From 8a5c6c1b21fbb4cab91facdd891aad59f1275a89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikita Poltorapavlo <Nikita_Poltorapavlo2@cable.comcast.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:18:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] RDKEMW-27354 : entservices-helpers contains duplicate
 definitons

Reason for change: Logging macros are expected to be defined only in
UtilsLogging.h. However at present they are also defined in utils.h.
Same for returnResponse, sendNotify macros (defined in UtilsJsonRpc.h), IARM
struct (defined in UtilsIarm.h), etc.
This needs to be fixed.
Original repo for rdkservices already had a refactored version of helpers where
"utils.h" and "utils.cpp" were eliminated to follow Separation of Concerns.
For some reason, they were copy-pasted from old codebase into RDK-E and now are
part of entservices-helpers along with new separated headers. "utils.h" and
"utils.cpp" contain duplicate definitons that already exist in other files
(UtilsLogging.h, UtilsIarm.h, ...) and thus unnecessary.
"utils.cpp" is the only translation module built by entservices-helpers as
shared library, thus by eliminating "utils.h" and "utils.cpp"
entservices-helpers package becomes INTERFACE library (no .so). No change is
needed to other components that use entservices-helpers, they will continue
linking entservices-helpers package but only headers will be used.
Pre-requisite for CPESP-10472
Test Procedure: None
Risks: Low
version: Patch
